{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, how can you say</b> — the meaning of 'how can you say' is addressed to his wicked enemies, and to them he speaks." "<b>Your mountain</b> — the mountain of yourselves." "<b>And a bird</b> — lacking a kaf, like 'a lion has roared' upon the watchtower of YHWH (Joel 1:6?), for it is like a lion; for HaShem is the one who roars and witnesses, the fact that it is upon the watchtower with three vowel points, for it is not in construct state; for the meaning is 'you say to my soul: flee of yourself to our mountain,' for you are like a bird, and behold the bow is drawn in darkness."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "The citation 'ויקרא אריה על מצפה ה' / a lion has roared upon the watchtower of YHWH' does not correspond to any standard verse exactly; possibly a conflation of Joel 1:6 or similar prophetic imagery. The argument about three vowel points on מצפה and the kafmissing in וצפור is textually dense and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:03.069399833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}